  "guidelines": {
    "modal_title": "Submission guidelines",
    "body": "1. Original work / authorization: Only submit content that is original or properly licensed. AI-generated images count as original (the prompt + parameters + output are yours). If you reference someone else's prompt, cite the source.\n\n2. Forbidden content: No explicit sexual content (NSFW), realistic violence or gore, hate speech or discrimination, disinformation (deepfakes of celebrities or politicians), content involving minors, privacy violations (real identifiable individuals), or clear copyright infringement (unauthorized use of well-known IP characters).\n\n3. Quality requirements: Bilingual prompts require at least one language to be complete (both title and prompt filled). Don't leave large chunks of English in the Chinese fields, or vice versa.\n\n4. Tags: Choose from existing tags, up to 6 per submission. Tags should accurately describe content (style / subject / composition / palette). Avoid marketing language or unrelated tags.\n\n5. Review process: Admins review manually, usually within 24 hours. The result will be delivered to you via in-site notification.\n\n6. Consequences: After 3 rejections, your daily quota drops from 10 to 5; serious violations may result in temporary suspension. Contact the site admin to appeal.",
